-  * `rm /1/var/lib/openlibrary/coverstore/items/l_cover_0008/l_covers_0008_00.*`
+Members are named `0008010042.jpg`, `0008010042-S.jpg`,
+`0008010042-M.jpg`, and `0008010042-L.jpg`, respectively. An uploaded
+cover's authoritative URL is
+`https://archive.org/download/covers_0008/covers_0008_01.zip/0008010042.jpg`.
+
+`archive.archive(test=False)` stages local images and sets `archived=true` with
+zip member references. The original images are removed once the closed zip
+files are staged and the database references are updated. Repeating the
+staging step does not add duplicate zip members. Missing local images set
+`failed=true` for investigation and do not enter a batch. Local batch locks
+serialize staging, upload, and finalization on one coverserver.
+
+After staging, call `Batch(8, 1).process_pending(upload=True, finalize=True)`.
+Upload is skipped for zip files already listed in their Internet Archive item.
+Finalization requires all four size archives to be listed remotely, then sets
+`uploaded=true`, replaces each filename with its archive.org URL, and removes
+the staged zip files. A failed upload or incomplete item leaves staging files
+and database state in place for retry. `test=True` skips upload, database
+finalization, and deletion. `archive.audit(8)` returns missing remote zip paths.
+
+Existing tar archives remain readable through the legacy coverstore path.
